#: src/conditional-expressions.md:1
msgid "Conditional Expressions"
msgstr ""

#: src/conditional-expressions.md:3
msgid ""
"`if`/`else` expressions evaluate different branches depending on if two "
"expressions evaluate to the same value:"
msgstr ""

#: src/conditional-expressions.md:6
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"foo := if \"2\" == \"2\" { \"Good!\" } else { \"1984\" }\n"
"\n"
"bar:\n"
"  @echo \"{{foo}}\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/conditional-expressions.md:18
msgid "It is also possible to test for inequality:"
msgstr ""

#: src/conditional-expressions.md:20
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"foo := if \"hello\" != \"goodbye\" { \"xyz\" } else { \"abc\" }\n"
"\n"
"bar:\n"
"  @echo {{foo}}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/conditional-expressions.md:32
msgid "And match against regular expressions:"
msgstr ""

#: src/conditional-expressions.md:34
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"foo := if \"hello\" =~ 'hel+o' { \"match\" } else { \"mismatch\" }\n"
"\n"
"bar:\n"
"  @echo {{foo}}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/conditional-expressions.md:46
msgid ""
"Regular expressions are provided by the [regex crate](https://github.com/"
"rust-lang/regex), whose syntax is documented on [docs.rs](https://docs.rs/"
"regex/1.5.4/regex/#syntax). Since regular expressions commonly use backslash "
"escape sequences, consider using single-quoted string literals, which will "
"pass slashes to the regex parser unmolested."
msgstr ""

#: src/conditional-expressions.md:52
msgid ""
"Conditional expressions short-circuit, which means they only evaluate one of "
"their branches. This can be used to make sure that backtick expressions "
"don’t run when they shouldn’t."
msgstr ""

#: src/conditional-expressions.md:56
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"foo := if env_var(\"RELEASE\") == \"true\" { `get-something-from-release-"
"database` } else { \"dummy-value\" }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/conditional-expressions.md:60
msgid "Conditionals can be used inside of recipes:"
msgstr ""

#: src/conditional-expressions.md:62
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"bar foo:\n"
"  echo {{ if foo == \"bar\" { \"hello\" } else { \"goodbye\" } }}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/conditional-expressions.md:67
msgid "Multiple conditionals can be chained:"
msgstr ""

#: src/conditional-expressions.md:69
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"foo := if \"hello\" == \"goodbye\" {\n"
"  \"xyz\"\n"
"} else if \"a\" == \"a\" {\n"
"  \"abc\"\n"
"} else {\n"
"  \"123\"\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"bar:\n"
"  @echo {{foo}}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
